> > What other tools will change into useful stuff when polyed?  I have
> > masses of tin whistles, mirrors and other useless stuff.

Objects will polymorph within the same class of object.  And, as
discussed above, generally speaking, non-magical tools will remain
non-magical and magical tools might or might not stay magical (60%).
That said, there are useful tools both magical and non-magical.  Some
of them however have significantly more worth in the early game, rather
than in the mid-game, which is when I tend to do my poly-piling.

So depending on what you need you might consider changing those
whistles and pick-axes into cans of grease, tinning kits, saddles,
stethoscopes, leashes (the poor man's magic whistle), lenses, maybe
even an ice box.  Read the tools spoiler list to see if there's
anything that you need.  Just make sure you're near your altar in case
you get an ice box since they're so heavy.  The downside to having so
much stuff to work with is that you run the risk of the higher return
items not changing.

I tend to make several piles of non-matching stuff and if a pile gets
low then I add a pick-axe or whistle and hope for something good.

Just don't put all of your pick-axes in one basket...or else they'll
hatch before you count 'em.



